8. The Windows synchronization logic contains a dangerous bug

This is particularly important:

git pull --rebase origin main

while you are on:

host-win-desktop

That means you're effectively saying:

current host branch
        +
main
        ↓
rebase

This undermines the clean host isolation you're trying to establish.

If the host branch is supposed to contain:

host-specific state

you need an explicit synchronization strategy.

I'd prefer:

fetch
 ↓
determine desired upstream
 ↓
reconcile
 ↓
apply
 ↓
commit
 ↓
push host branch

rather than an unconditional:

git pull --rebase origin main


