10. The CI design is currently too weak

Your CI has the right intention:

> ShellCheck + pristine bootstrap testing. 



But this:

echo "ci-test-runner" | ./scripts/bootstrap.sh

does not constitute a clean bootstrap test.

Why?

Because the script still depends on things like:

Git identity
GitHub authentication
remote repository
GNU Stow
filesystem state
existing home directory
branch state
OS detection
permissions

A stronger CI architecture would be:

PR
                     │
          ┌──────────┴──────────┐
          ▼                     ▼
      static tests          integration
          │                     │
     ShellCheck            container/VM
     shfmt                  clean HOME
     YAML lint              clean repo
     policy tests           bootstrap
          │                     │
          └──────────┬──────────┘
                     ▼
                 PR gate


